        "paragraphs": [
            "Gemma is a family of generative artificial intelligence models from Google that you can use in a wide variety of generation tasks, including question answering, summarization, and reasoning. Google says Gemma models are provided with open weights and permit responsible commercial use, allowing you to tune and deploy them in your own projects and applications. The family includes a range of model sizes, capabilities, and task-specialized variations to help you build custom generative solutions.",
            "The latest generation is Gemma 4, which Google says spans four distinct architectures: Small Sizes, Dense, Mixture-of-Experts, and Unified. Gemma 4 models are available in 5 parameter sizes: E2B, E4B, 12B, 31B and 26B A4B. Earlier versions of Gemma core models are also available, including Gemma 3, Gemma 2, and Gemma 1. The family also includes special-purpose and research models such as PaliGemma, ShieldGemma, EmbeddingGemma, FunctionGemma, and others.",
            "You can download Gemma 4 models from Kaggle and Hugging Face. Google says a good place to start is the Gemma 4 26B A4B model in the latest available version, which can be used for many tasks and has lower resource requirements. Gemma models are compatible with a wide variety of ecosystem tools, and you can run them locally with a Chat UI, build and train in Python, deploy on mobile and edge devices, or deploy to production and enterprise environments."
        ],
